## What to deliver

Build and rig the foundry up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a tall masonry works with a broad radar dish
crowning it and a heavy piston on its flank. **Author the two required animations**
as F-curves with the `voxel-anim` animation subcommands: `dish_sweep` (the dish
turning one full, smooth revolution about its vertical axis) and `piston_bob` (the
piston driving straight down and rising back up with weight into the drop and the
recovery) — both self-playing idles that run continuously on their own while the
works body stays fixed. The animations are the fixed contract — produce both, by
those names; the parts and joints that realize them are yours. When you are
satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished
submission.
